            <ArticleTitle>Sacral neuromodulation stimulation for IC/PBS, chronic pelvic pain, and sexual dysfunction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1553-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00192-010-1281-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study aims to review the use of sacral neuromodulation in the patient population with painful bladder syndrome/interstitial cystitis (PBS/IC), chronic pelvic pain (CPP), and sexual dysfunction. A literature review of the current research was carried out. This article highlights the current research findings and uses of sacral neuromodulation in patients with PBS/IC, CPP, vulvar vestibulitis, and erectile dysfunction. Current research on sacral neuromodulation on the abovementioned patient population has shown potential efficacy in pilot studies, though larger, multi-centered trials with long-term follow-up are needed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
